# Heiken — Netlify SPA fallback.
# React Router owns the routes (/login, /library, /watch/..., etc.). On a
# static host every unknown path must serve the app shell (index.html), or
# reloading/deep-linking shows Netlify's "Page not found".
# API paths are NOT rewritten — the engine lives elsewhere (VITE_API_BASE_URL).
# Explicit 404 for /api/* on Netlify so the client can detect that the baked
# base is wrong and prompt the user to set the server override, instead of
# serving index.html (200) which would be parsed as JSON and confuse errors.
/api/* /api/:splat 404
/* /index.html 200
